+## Forward V19-O dedicated lab anchor owner
+
+This candidate keeps the broker, transition, COMMIT, replay and V19
+reader-recovery bodies unchanged. The owned fixture moves the anchor schema,
+two tables and fixed lock broker to a dedicated NOLOGIN owner. It grants
+the distinct sealed native owner only anchor USAGE, table SELECT and exact
+broker EXECUTE. The anchor owner receives no native object rights, and runtime
+actors cannot assume either owner. Exact grantors, ownership, privileges and
+both owner roles are checked before capturing instance-specific catalog gold.
+
+The catalog includes the anchor owner's attributes and inbound/outbound
+membership edges. V19's exact one-writer recovery exception remains unchanged
+and cannot normalize owner drift. The new case proves actual actor assumption
+and fresh owner-login denial, successful broker-mediated installation, and
+rollback-only owner attribute/membership drift refusal with unchanged evidence.
+
+This remains a private superuser-bootstrap laboratory. Managed creator edges,
+getter-only grants, finite credentials, general retirement and hosted adoption
+are out of scope. This source candidate has not been executed.
+
+## Composition V20-O: dedicated anchor owner and one terminal batch
+
+The dedicated NOLOGIN anchor owner owns the schema, both anchor tables and
+fixed row-lock broker. The distinct NOLOGIN sealed owner has only anchor
+USAGE, SELECT and broker EXECUTE, granted from that anchor owner. No actor
+can assume either owner or write the retirement marker. The broker has no
+DML, role-management statement or dynamic SQL.
+
+Only the existing disposable fixture bootstrap superuser issues the
+closed atomic retirement arrangement. It checks its own session identity,
+exact scope, package, roles and original Stop under the same locks. The
+dedicated anchor owner receives no role-management right, and no persistent
+membership or grant is introduced for the bootstrap superuser. Intrinsic
+anchor table ownership is isolated by NOLOGIN, no memberships and the
+fixed broker entry. The bootstrap superuser remains the trusted
+administrative boundary of the owned fixture.
+
+The full held catalog additionally pins the dedicated owner and all its
+membership edges. The V20 terminal projection still changes only the two
+pinned writer login bits. The accepted package needs a fresh independently
+verified constructor and exact seal before the synthetic transition.
+
+All 41 combined test methods are preserved byte for byte. The two new
+focused methods from the parent slices are selected for the first
+composed native run. This composition has only static verification so far.
